WEBVTT

00:15.360 --> 00:21.300
♪ Through the mist, we walk side by side
across endless mountains and seas ♪

00:21.900 --> 00:25.120
♪ Each sunrise brings hope,
and every sunset answers in kind ♪

00:25.890 --> 00:28.750
♪ Drawn by the heart's call ♪

00:30.040 --> 00:36.050
♪ We brave wind and frost,
free beneath the boundless sky ♪

00:36.750 --> 00:40.220
♪ Every moonrise glows with pure radiance,
and every moonset fades into a dream ♪

00:40.830 --> 00:44.620
♪ In the years to come, I'll ponder it ♪

00:46.320 --> 00:49.440
♪ Across the vast mortal world,
our spirits soaring high ♪

00:49.980 --> 00:53.210
♪ We vowed to forge ahead together ♪

00:53.730 --> 00:55.110
♪ After weathering life's storms ♪

00:55.640 --> 01:00.840
♪ I look back on our days
of youth and freedom ♪

01:01.240 --> 01:04.500
♪ Now rusted by time,
swallowed by a boundless crimson tide ♪

01:05.090 --> 01:08.110
♪ All love and hatred in this world
mean nothing anymore ♪

01:08.590 --> 01:09.900
♪ A life of highs and lows ♪

01:10.480 --> 01:16.150
♪ Yet never shared with you ♪

02:42.970 --> 02:49.450
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

02:49.770 --> 02:52.500
[Episode 9]

03:00.300 --> 03:01.050
How did it go?

03:01.250 --> 03:02.580
Did you find the killer?

03:03.130 --> 03:04.050
Cousin...

03:04.730 --> 03:05.780
I've been poisoned.

03:05.780 --> 03:06.960
Yeah, I know.

03:06.970 --> 03:08.300
But aren't you the "Plague"?

03:08.300 --> 03:09.900
Isn't this part of your plan?

03:13.050 --> 03:13.800
Run.

03:13.910 --> 03:16.240
They're coming for us! They're coming...

03:25.350 --> 03:27.030
It's time to settle this once and for all.

03:25.420 --> 03:27.710
[A ball will be held
in the upper-deck VIP suite.]

03:31.550 --> 03:33.050
Clean the area.

03:33.130 --> 03:35.070
I'm going out for a while.

03:35.400 --> 03:39.040
There is a violent chicken
from the lower hold.

03:35.510 --> 03:39.650
[Best regards, Dong Zhuohua]

03:39.070 --> 03:40.579
Don't go out.

03:41.620 --> 03:43.480
What's the point of staying here?

03:44.090 --> 03:45.650
Danger will find me anyway.

03:45.930 --> 03:46.740
So,

03:47.900 --> 03:49.530
I'm going to take a walk

03:50.000 --> 03:53.290
and see if anything new happens.

04:29.580 --> 04:31.980
Tonight's dinner was actually quite good.

05:30.980 --> 05:32.730
What did I do wrong?

05:34.690 --> 05:36.930
Why do I have to go through all this crap?

05:47.730 --> 05:50.320
Maybe it's precisely
because you did nothing wrong

05:50.320 --> 05:51.780
that you're going through all this.

05:51.780 --> 05:52.909
It's all your fault.

05:54.610 --> 05:55.870
Ever since I met you...

05:57.600 --> 05:59.510
I don't know who I'll run into

05:59.540 --> 06:02.340
or what will happen
when I open my eyes the next day.

06:02.350 --> 06:04.680
My life wasn't supposed to be like this...

06:07.690 --> 06:09.220
Well, now that you're here,

06:09.780 --> 06:11.550
welcome to my world.

06:12.870 --> 06:14.470
Why don't we sit down and talk

06:14.830 --> 06:15.730
about

06:15.760 --> 06:16.740
what to do next?

06:17.850 --> 06:20.110
Let's eat something
to replenish our strength.

06:20.110 --> 06:21.020
Again?

06:26.010 --> 06:27.340
Better safe than sorry.

06:29.020 --> 06:29.820
First of all,

06:30.010 --> 06:32.010
this is a very meticulous plan.

06:32.310 --> 06:34.100
Our opponents
are definitely professionals.

06:34.100 --> 06:34.830
But I didn't expect

06:34.830 --> 06:36.360
them to have so many people.

06:36.550 --> 06:37.750
I told you.

06:38.040 --> 06:39.130
I warned you.

06:39.150 --> 06:40.550
But you wouldn't listen.

06:49.370 --> 06:50.970
When we entered first class,

06:51.070 --> 06:52.190
they all saw us.

06:52.540 --> 06:54.340
So they will definitely follow us here.

06:54.340 --> 06:55.630
But not too soon,

06:56.100 --> 06:58.230
because they don't know
which room we're in.

06:58.230 --> 06:59.360
This is first class,

06:59.560 --> 07:00.440
not third class.

07:00.440 --> 07:01.950
The security isn't even comparable.

07:01.950 --> 07:03.410
They won't attack rashly.

07:03.570 --> 07:05.190
Most likely, they've arranged men
at the exits

07:05.190 --> 07:06.250
to keep an eye on us.

07:06.430 --> 07:07.830
We can't get out anymore.

07:08.820 --> 07:10.080
There are also killers

07:10.220 --> 07:11.420
among the waitstaff.

07:11.620 --> 07:13.550
So they'll sweep room by room.

07:14.100 --> 07:16.300
At the latest, they'll find us tonight.

07:19.250 --> 07:19.810
Look,

07:20.250 --> 07:21.770
it's almost 9 o'clock.

07:21.770 --> 07:22.570
Don't worry.

07:23.890 --> 07:25.230
I'll find a way out.

07:48.650 --> 07:49.480
Shh.

07:51.690 --> 07:52.420
Who's there?

07:53.210 --> 07:55.610
I'm here to deliver the invitation letter.

07:56.380 --> 07:57.420
I'm showering.

07:57.520 --> 07:59.620
Just put it in through the door crack.

08:07.830 --> 08:08.690
Yes, sir.

08:22.070 --> 08:24.540
[Invitation]

08:23.520 --> 08:24.200
What is it?

08:24.540 --> 08:25.750
[Mr. Steven, you are cordially invited to
attend tomorrow evening at 9:00 PM.]

08:28.010 --> 08:29.450
Our last card to play.

08:29.610 --> 08:33.669
[Best regards, Dong Zhuohua]

08:30.740 --> 08:32.200
The ship owner, Miss Dong.

08:32.460 --> 08:33.500
Miss Dong?

08:33.980 --> 08:37.350
[We await your gracious presence.]

08:37.500 --> 08:38.409
Zhang Hailou,

08:38.970 --> 08:40.460
I've let you investigate for so long.

08:40.460 --> 08:42.440
[Best regards, Dong Zhuohua]

08:41.049 --> 08:42.650
It's time to close the net.

08:43.570 --> 08:45.210
It seems fate hasn't abandoned me.

08:45.210 --> 08:46.980
Heaven is still on my side.

08:48.290 --> 08:50.060
So you're saying

08:50.130 --> 08:51.170
Miss Dong

08:51.170 --> 08:52.650
can help us catch the bad guys?

08:52.650 --> 08:53.530
Of course.

08:55.350 --> 08:57.320
But those bad guys have seen your face.

08:57.320 --> 08:58.770
You can't even go out now.

08:59.910 --> 09:01.780
So I need some time to prepare.

09:05.390 --> 09:07.810
Are you sure Miss Dong can help you?

09:08.450 --> 09:09.860
Those people have hidden themselves well.

09:08.780 --> 09:11.590
[These are the bandits on your ship.]

09:09.900 --> 09:11.190
Even if you manage to see her,

09:11.190 --> 09:12.280
why would she believe you?

09:11.610 --> 09:15.190
[Check it, and you'll know I'm not lying.]

09:12.650 --> 09:14.450
Who said I need her to believe me?

09:15.530 --> 09:17.330
Right now, all I need is one dance

09:17.900 --> 09:18.830
with Miss Dong.

09:21.050 --> 09:21.650
It seems

09:21.650 --> 09:22.770
the deal you made last time

09:22.770 --> 09:23.900
was quite a good one.

09:26.460 --> 09:28.260
We must seize this opportunity.

09:29.290 --> 09:29.740
Please come in.

09:29.740 --> 09:30.470
Give it to me.

09:30.620 --> 09:31.200
Please.

09:33.230 --> 09:34.560
With that face of yours,

09:34.720 --> 09:36.320
you'll be spotted
the moment you walk out the door.

09:36.320 --> 09:38.250
How are you going to get to the ball?

09:39.090 --> 09:41.770
It's indeed hard to disguise yourself
as a foreigner,

09:41.770 --> 09:43.170
but changing appearance

09:43.530 --> 09:45.930
is a skill I've practiced since childhood.

10:28.530 --> 10:30.720
This ball looks pretty extravagant.

10:31.250 --> 10:33.010
When will Miss Dong appear?

11:19.350 --> 11:22.080
Steven, my friend,
where have you been all night?

11:23.370 --> 11:24.800
I had a bad sore throat.

11:25.400 --> 11:27.400
Needed to go back to get my medicine.

11:27.440 --> 11:29.100
You don't need your throat to dance.

11:29.100 --> 11:30.490
Come on, let's finish dinner.

11:30.490 --> 11:31.570
Have some fun.

11:31.910 --> 11:32.880
I'd love to.

11:40.190 --> 11:42.490
I hear they have some special wine here

11:42.590 --> 11:43.930
for dance parties.

11:49.940 --> 11:50.770
Steven?

11:55.050 --> 11:55.940
Miss Dong,

11:55.940 --> 11:57.010
have you made up your mind

11:57.010 --> 11:58.650
about the matter I mentioned last time?

11:58.650 --> 11:59.620
As I said,

12:00.110 --> 12:02.010
the deal we agreed upon
when we boarded this ship

12:02.010 --> 12:03.250
is final.

12:03.890 --> 12:05.020
I can't accommodate

12:05.220 --> 12:06.680
your additional demands.

12:07.650 --> 12:08.960
They aren't additional demands.

12:08.960 --> 12:10.990
It's an additional deal.

12:11.170 --> 12:13.940
This is a piece of jade
discovered in Central Asia,

12:13.940 --> 12:16.480
the crown jewel of my collection.

12:16.510 --> 12:19.280
I hope it can open the door

12:19.390 --> 12:21.450
to a broader partnership between us.

12:22.170 --> 12:24.500
An opportunity delivered to my doorstep.

12:26.580 --> 12:28.110
It's indeed very precious.

12:28.170 --> 12:30.500
But exchanging it for the entry documents

12:30.940 --> 12:33.130
means letting our family risk our lives

12:33.130 --> 12:34.340
for a stone.

12:35.100 --> 12:37.160
I'm afraid my father wouldn't agree.

12:37.170 --> 12:39.500
Besides, I haven't reached Xiacheng yet.

12:40.010 --> 12:42.350
Our first deal hasn't been completed.

12:42.770 --> 12:43.890
So, why the rush?

12:45.150 --> 12:46.370
By the time we reach Xiacheng,

12:46.370 --> 12:48.490
I'm afraid one stone won't be enough.

12:48.930 --> 12:49.770
What I mean is,

12:49.770 --> 12:51.530
you accept this stone now,

12:52.070 --> 12:53.800
send a telegram to your father,

12:53.890 --> 12:55.170
and help us get

12:55.170 --> 12:57.280
the entry and exit documents
before we arrive in Xiacheng.

12:57.280 --> 12:58.730
Once we arrive

12:58.750 --> 13:00.900
and secure the treasure
indicated on the map,

13:00.900 --> 13:02.700
you can take back the documents.

13:05.170 --> 13:06.430
You're trying to use me

13:06.650 --> 13:07.910
to threaten my father?

13:25.070 --> 13:27.970
It's a deal, Miss Dong. A deal.

13:28.220 --> 13:29.260
Mr. Warner,

13:30.760 --> 13:31.670
you said

13:32.770 --> 13:35.370
your men are all cold-blooded killers,

13:35.370 --> 13:36.030
right?

13:36.410 --> 13:38.930
Yes, cold-blooded killers

13:39.170 --> 13:40.750
at my command.

13:40.820 --> 13:41.940
Right, Steven?

13:44.120 --> 13:45.960
I need to distract the armed guards
at the door first

13:45.960 --> 13:47.960
to have a chance to kidnap Miss Dong.

13:49.120 --> 13:50.080
Miss Dong,

13:50.340 --> 13:52.470
you've been stalling for far too long.

13:52.670 --> 13:54.480
Give me your answer today.

13:54.480 --> 13:55.420
Otherwise,

13:55.440 --> 13:57.120
we may all face quite a fright

13:57.120 --> 13:58.630
tonight.

13:58.630 --> 14:00.630
Then you'll certainly be frightened.

14:00.630 --> 14:01.910
Mr. Fake Face,

14:01.910 --> 14:03.510
do you think you'll succeed?

14:19.840 --> 14:20.840
She's so fierce.

14:20.860 --> 14:22.660
A shipping magnate's daughter?

14:22.920 --> 14:26.320
She's exactly the kind of daughter
I would've raised myself.

14:26.870 --> 14:29.510
I'm here to report my findings.

14:29.550 --> 14:30.870
I've found those bandits.

14:30.870 --> 14:32.270
Here are their sketches.

15:37.270 --> 15:38.400
Zhang Hailou,

15:38.540 --> 15:40.270
your disguise skills are good.

15:40.270 --> 15:42.110
Too bad I taught you.

15:42.500 --> 15:44.430
So I saw through it at first glance.

15:51.360 --> 15:52.820
What's wrong with Steven?

15:54.510 --> 15:55.740
Where's my jade?

15:55.760 --> 15:58.750
Your jade was stolen by Steven.

15:59.750 --> 16:01.510
What the hell is going on with Steven?

16:01.510 --> 16:03.460
He's jumping around like a monkey.

16:03.770 --> 16:06.370
Miss Dong, I lost something on your ship.

16:06.510 --> 16:07.750
You should take responsibility for it.

16:07.750 --> 16:09.080
That's not quite right.

16:09.180 --> 16:10.960
Wasn't it your man who stole it?

16:13.390 --> 16:15.290
You've tried to fool me.

16:15.600 --> 16:17.410
That guy just now was not Steven at all.

16:17.410 --> 16:19.120
If Steven could jump down from here

16:19.120 --> 16:19.840
and still run away,

16:19.840 --> 16:21.220
I'd lick your boots.

16:29.840 --> 16:32.170
Since the thief's objective was the jade,

16:32.510 --> 16:34.410
it must still be on the ship

16:34.930 --> 16:36.580
before we dock.

16:36.870 --> 16:38.400
What are you worried about?

16:40.870 --> 16:42.560
Conduct a search now.

16:43.240 --> 16:45.000
Announce this to everyone

16:45.510 --> 16:48.120
and have all passengers
remain in their rooms

16:48.700 --> 16:51.010
to await Mr. Warner's inspection.

16:52.220 --> 16:54.420
What exactly is this woman trying to do?

16:56.550 --> 16:58.350
Attention, all passengers.

16:58.510 --> 17:01.370
The Nan'an has entered
an emergency ship lockdown.

17:01.480 --> 17:03.870
Please return to your cabins immediately.

17:03.870 --> 17:05.069
Do not visit other rooms

17:05.069 --> 17:06.780
or host overnight guests.

17:06.880 --> 17:09.250
Violators will be treated as stowaways.

17:14.640 --> 17:16.510
Attention, all passengers.

17:16.510 --> 17:19.869
The Nan'an has entered
an emergency ship lockdown.

17:20.109 --> 17:21.440
Please return to your rooms immediately.

17:21.440 --> 17:22.770
Do not visit other rooms

17:22.790 --> 17:24.680
or host overnight guests.

17:24.700 --> 17:25.569
I don't know.

17:25.880 --> 17:27.180
I heard there are bandits on the ship.

17:27.180 --> 17:29.230
It's dangerous,
so they've locked the ship down.

17:29.230 --> 17:30.960
I also heard that during the lockdown,

17:30.960 --> 17:32.270
anyone not in their cabin
will be arrested—

17:32.270 --> 17:34.350
regardless of whether they're a suspect.

17:34.350 --> 17:36.610
Miss Dong, if you can't recover the jade,

17:36.610 --> 17:38.220
we may not be going to Xiacheng.

17:38.220 --> 17:39.510
Miss Dong, your father

17:39.510 --> 17:42.040
will have to offer more
to get the ship to dock.

17:42.780 --> 17:44.030
I see that jade

17:44.030 --> 17:45.830
wasn't even yours to begin with.

17:46.400 --> 17:48.730
You borrowed it from a museum, didn't you?

17:49.090 --> 17:50.440
Using a borrowed item
to make your own deal...

17:50.440 --> 17:52.300
Does the museum know your tricks?

17:52.440 --> 17:53.720
It doesn't matter

17:53.720 --> 17:55.660
whose hands a museum's jade is kept in.

17:55.660 --> 17:58.180
Trading a few priceless treasures

17:58.310 --> 17:59.910
for entry and exit documents

18:00.230 --> 18:01.710
is certainly a good deal.

18:01.730 --> 18:03.970
But losing them? That's another matter.

18:03.970 --> 18:04.650
Indeed.

18:05.480 --> 18:07.610
Then you'd become a wanted man abroad,

18:07.790 --> 18:09.950
and your academic reputation
would be destroyed.

18:09.950 --> 18:11.000
Simply put,

18:11.400 --> 18:12.830
without that jade,

18:13.240 --> 18:14.500
you're finished.

18:16.130 --> 18:18.100
It means we share the same fate.

18:18.270 --> 18:20.360
Wouldn't you agree, Mr. Warner?

18:21.590 --> 18:23.650
Give me command of your armed unit.

18:23.880 --> 18:24.920
Tonight,

18:24.920 --> 18:26.650
I'll help you recover the jade.

18:26.960 --> 18:28.420
As for the rest of our deal,

18:28.550 --> 18:30.010
we can talk about it later.

18:31.350 --> 18:31.830
Okay.

18:36.290 --> 18:37.030
Gentlemen,

18:37.750 --> 18:39.350
there are no rules here.

18:39.660 --> 18:41.310
Anyone I tell you to kill,

18:41.750 --> 18:43.270
shoot them right away.

18:43.640 --> 18:46.920
Otherwise, I can't guarantee your safety.

18:49.760 --> 18:51.490
Let's go. Check Steven's room.

19:19.310 --> 19:20.680
That man just told me

19:21.510 --> 19:23.440
to give this money to... who was it?

19:23.630 --> 19:25.160
Give this money

19:25.200 --> 19:26.610
to Zhang Hailou.

19:26.850 --> 19:27.820
Forget it.

19:29.400 --> 19:30.310
I'm in enough trouble as it is.

19:30.310 --> 19:32.840
Why get involved in
someone else's business?

19:33.000 --> 19:36.060
I'll just hand it to the ship police
before getting off.

19:46.880 --> 19:47.830
What

19:47.830 --> 19:49.480
rotten luck, day after day.

19:56.310 --> 19:57.070
He's back.

20:17.200 --> 20:18.590
What are you doing here?

20:23.310 --> 20:25.120
What the hell are you doing here?

20:27.830 --> 20:30.750
No, not me! It has nothing to do with me!

20:30.750 --> 20:31.160
No!

20:31.160 --> 20:31.680
Wait.

20:32.750 --> 20:33.960
Take him to the room.

20:36.200 --> 20:36.810
Get up!

20:53.670 --> 20:56.040
These are the bandits on your ship.

20:56.240 --> 20:58.440
Check it, and you'll know I'm not lying.

20:58.680 --> 21:00.740
I've found the bandits.

21:33.160 --> 21:35.350
[Telegram]

21:53.830 --> 21:55.420
I've already verified it.

21:55.650 --> 21:56.850
He's the real Steven.

21:57.240 --> 21:58.570
He didn't take the jade.

22:00.120 --> 22:01.450
Then who stole the jade?

22:01.790 --> 22:03.350
It was that con man surnamed Zhang.

22:03.350 --> 22:04.440
I was kidnapped by him.

22:04.440 --> 22:06.700
-He knows the face-changing art.
-Blaming everything on me, huh?

22:06.700 --> 22:08.250
Blaming whoever is absent, huh?

22:08.250 --> 22:10.270
But I don't know what his real purpose is.

22:10.270 --> 22:11.240
Now it seems

22:11.240 --> 22:13.440
the jade was what he was after all along.

22:14.790 --> 22:16.270
This man is his accomplice.

22:16.270 --> 22:17.200
Miss Dong,

22:17.350 --> 22:18.930
since this man is his accomplice,

22:18.930 --> 22:21.070
how do you think we should deal with him?

22:21.070 --> 22:21.790
Kill him.

22:24.440 --> 22:24.840
You...

22:25.200 --> 22:27.750
It seems she's not bluffing.

22:27.750 --> 22:29.070
That young man named Zhang

22:29.070 --> 22:30.480
isn't working with her.

22:31.310 --> 22:33.110
So, what should we do with him now?

22:33.110 --> 22:34.000
Hudson.

22:34.310 --> 22:35.370
You know what to do.

22:36.510 --> 22:37.310
Turn around.

22:37.310 --> 22:37.880
No!

22:38.040 --> 22:39.770
-Don't look at me!
-Please, no!

22:39.960 --> 22:40.510
Hudson,

22:41.000 --> 22:41.680
easy.

22:42.510 --> 22:43.830
We should spare him for now.

22:43.830 --> 22:46.030
In case that woman is trying to embezzle

22:46.070 --> 22:47.870
and wants to get rid of a witness.

22:49.850 --> 22:51.240
Bring him downstairs.

22:51.480 --> 22:52.030
Come on.

23:28.270 --> 23:30.400
They've really started killing
without restraint.

23:30.400 --> 23:32.570
[Go up and down the auxiliary ladders
steadily and slowly.]

23:35.760 --> 23:37.820
The whole ship is hunting for you now.

23:37.850 --> 23:39.480
Could you not just listen to me for once?

23:39.480 --> 23:40.750
If you keep wasting time,

23:40.750 --> 23:42.070
you'll be the one to die.

23:42.070 --> 23:42.590
What?

23:44.040 --> 23:45.460
How do you still
have the nerve to say that?

23:45.460 --> 23:46.810
You actually think you're justified here?

23:46.810 --> 23:48.380
They're clearly trying to arrest you!

23:48.380 --> 23:50.090
What does it have to do with me?

23:50.090 --> 23:51.730
I was taken hostage by you!

23:51.770 --> 23:52.570
You... you...

23:54.590 --> 23:55.590
Are you okay?

23:57.050 --> 23:59.230
I-I won't say anything more, alright?

23:59.530 --> 24:00.880
So, what do we do now?

24:03.030 --> 24:03.790
Stay alive.

24:05.010 --> 24:06.410
If we remain on this ship,

24:06.880 --> 24:08.700
we'll just end up
being killed by Miss Dong.

24:08.700 --> 24:11.110
There are people everywhere
on the ship now.

24:11.110 --> 24:13.040
We'll get caught wherever we hide.

24:15.640 --> 24:16.830
The Apple Theory.

24:17.420 --> 24:18.590
Ever heard of it?

24:20.110 --> 24:21.450
I don't like apples!

24:21.510 --> 24:23.040
Who the hell asked you that?

24:29.030 --> 24:30.590
I only made enough food for one person.

24:30.590 --> 24:31.980
I'll ask you two a question.

24:31.260 --> 24:33.400
[Young Zhang Hailou] [Young Zhang Haixia]

24:32.110 --> 24:34.040
Whoever answers first gets to eat.

24:39.850 --> 24:42.510
And don't you two little brats
secretly team up.

24:43.750 --> 24:44.810
Listen carefully.

24:45.830 --> 24:47.760
These apples on the table are mine.

24:48.310 --> 24:49.270
You two

24:49.270 --> 24:51.350
need to steal the apples from here.

24:51.510 --> 24:52.750
Both of you have to steal some

24:52.750 --> 24:54.240
and figure out a way
without making me suspicious.

24:54.240 --> 24:56.440
Think individually. No conspiring.

25:05.900 --> 25:08.460
I'd give six apples to Zhang Hailou

25:08.790 --> 25:09.990
and let him run first.

25:10.720 --> 25:12.750
Then I'd stay here with the last apple.

25:12.750 --> 25:13.880
After you came back,

25:14.200 --> 25:15.320
I'd tell you

25:15.550 --> 25:17.810
that Zhang Hailou took all seven apples.

25:18.440 --> 25:19.140
Why?

25:19.520 --> 25:21.720
Because as far as
Zhang Hailou is concerned,

25:21.720 --> 25:24.490
whether he took six or seven,

25:24.920 --> 25:26.510
you'd already be furious.

25:27.030 --> 25:28.240
You'd just assume

25:28.590 --> 25:30.030
that he took

25:30.030 --> 25:31.200
all seven apples.

25:31.550 --> 25:33.270
And he wouldn't bother clarifying

25:33.270 --> 25:35.070
exactly how many he really took,

25:35.070 --> 25:36.830
because getting a beating

25:36.830 --> 25:38.630
would be inevitable either way.

25:38.680 --> 25:39.750
Zhang Haixia,

25:40.000 --> 25:41.020
you beast!

25:41.200 --> 25:43.590
You'd actually come up
with a scheme like that?

25:43.590 --> 25:44.790
I was just thinking of

25:45.070 --> 25:46.310
pinning the whole thing

25:46.310 --> 25:48.220
on Ergou next door!

25:54.830 --> 25:55.700
Zhang Hailou,

25:56.030 --> 25:57.360
when you're hungry,

25:57.400 --> 25:59.270
think carefully about this lesson.

25:59.270 --> 26:01.510
Someday, when you find yourself
in a tight spot,

26:01.510 --> 26:04.040
you must know
how to get yourself off the hook.

26:16.220 --> 26:17.080
Eat up quickly.

26:18.510 --> 26:20.200
Finish it before our mentor finds out.

26:20.200 --> 26:22.260
Otherwise, we'll both be in trouble.

26:38.580 --> 26:39.820
Hide here for 20 minutes.

26:39.820 --> 26:42.280
I'll go take care of something
and come back.

26:42.940 --> 26:43.790
You're injured this badly.

26:43.790 --> 26:45.190
Where are you even going?

26:45.240 --> 26:47.470
I'm going to find some corpses
and save your sorry life.

26:47.470 --> 26:48.590
It's so dangerous out there.

26:48.590 --> 26:50.120
Why bother looking for one?

26:50.320 --> 26:52.160
With your injury,
if you keep pushing yourself,

26:52.160 --> 26:53.450
you'll become a corpse, you know?

26:53.450 --> 26:55.080
Miss Dong now sees us as a threat.

26:55.080 --> 26:56.000
With her personality,

26:56.000 --> 26:57.240
after she finishes off all the killers,

26:57.240 --> 26:59.110
she'll definitely take a headcount
of everyone on the ship.

26:59.110 --> 26:59.960
Then she'll find us

26:59.960 --> 27:00.960
and kill us.

27:01.070 --> 27:02.000
Then what do we do?

27:02.000 --> 27:03.600
So, I need to find two decoys.

27:03.720 --> 27:04.530
Throw them onto a lifeboat

27:04.530 --> 27:05.830
and make it look like they escaped.

27:05.830 --> 27:07.310
That way, Miss Dong will
jump to the conclusion

27:07.310 --> 27:08.590
that we fled by boat as well.

27:08.590 --> 27:10.390
It's just like the Apple Theory.

27:11.110 --> 27:13.030
I can't follow what you're saying.

27:13.030 --> 27:15.360
The way your mind works
is just not normal.

27:15.750 --> 27:17.790
We're being hunted right now,

27:17.790 --> 27:19.750
and your solution is
to go back and kill people.

27:19.750 --> 27:21.280
You're absolutely insane.

27:21.750 --> 27:23.270
Taking Miss Dong hostage
is a lost cause now.

27:23.270 --> 27:24.480
You don't understand.

27:24.480 --> 27:26.550
This is exactly
the most unexpected approach

27:26.550 --> 27:28.190
for us to remain on the ship

27:28.510 --> 27:29.680
and reach Xiacheng safely,

27:29.680 --> 27:30.750
then return to Nanyang
as quickly as possible.

27:30.750 --> 27:31.500
You guys,

27:31.960 --> 27:33.090
go check over there.

27:33.270 --> 27:33.750
You!

27:34.030 --> 27:35.140
You guys, this way.

27:48.290 --> 27:50.420
Stay here and wait for me to come back.

28:05.070 --> 28:07.130
How could I have forgotten about you?

28:08.510 --> 28:10.620
At last, this moment has come.

28:12.360 --> 28:14.490
It's time to settle things between us.

28:17.890 --> 28:19.100
Believe it or not,

28:20.000 --> 28:21.990
people who say that

28:22.900 --> 28:24.030
usually end up dead.

28:27.990 --> 28:29.170
Zhang,

28:29.320 --> 28:31.450
I said I would kill you sooner or later!

28:31.680 --> 28:33.000
It just took a little longer
than expected.

28:33.000 --> 28:35.530
But now I'm going to
make good on that promise.

28:36.400 --> 28:37.010
Come on.

28:37.090 --> 28:38.090
What are you looking at?

28:38.090 --> 28:38.900
Stop looking around!

28:38.900 --> 28:40.760
There's nothing here to save you.

28:41.610 --> 28:43.250
All your dirty tricks

28:43.250 --> 28:44.370
won't work here.

28:45.100 --> 28:46.180
Do you still remember?

28:46.180 --> 28:47.510
The blades in your mouth

28:47.790 --> 28:49.390
aren't as fast as my bullets.

28:50.550 --> 28:52.440
After all, you're
the fastest gun in Nanyang.

28:52.440 --> 28:54.100
Let's talk this out calmly...

28:55.790 --> 28:57.960
I originally wanted to
shoot you dead with one bullet,

28:57.960 --> 28:58.590
but that

28:59.270 --> 29:00.670
would be too easy for you.

29:01.700 --> 29:03.680
The suffering I've endured
these past few days—

29:03.680 --> 29:05.340
you need to experience it too.

29:05.720 --> 29:06.680
Jump.

29:08.720 --> 29:09.660
I heard that

29:09.690 --> 29:12.120
when someone gets pulled into
a high-speed turbine,

29:12.120 --> 29:14.180
they only stay alive
for about two seconds.

29:14.180 --> 29:16.990
But those two seconds are pure agony.

29:18.890 --> 29:20.760
I haven't finished yet!

29:21.310 --> 29:22.300
Look over there.

29:24.410 --> 29:26.160
Come on, you idiots!

29:34.240 --> 29:35.080
Jesus.

29:35.250 --> 29:36.960
Someone's firing from an ambush!

29:36.960 --> 29:37.730
This Steven

29:37.750 --> 29:38.750
is wearing a mask!

29:58.140 --> 30:01.540
There are three men in the portrait
retreating into the hold.

30:02.590 --> 30:03.960
Use the projectiles.

30:03.960 --> 30:05.020
Where is Miss Dong?

30:05.110 --> 30:06.970
Miss Dong, she wouldn't let us in.

30:07.000 --> 30:08.710
She handled this by herself.

30:31.630 --> 30:34.290
Looks like the killers are
all in the cargo hold.

30:47.200 --> 30:48.140
Shh.

30:53.660 --> 30:54.900
Don't make a sound.

30:55.290 --> 30:57.420
Let's settle this with our fists, bro.

31:55.010 --> 31:56.160
No way.

31:59.790 --> 32:00.550
Plague?

32:02.200 --> 32:03.100
Plague?

32:04.510 --> 32:05.610
Plague?

32:11.830 --> 32:12.760
Why are you here?

32:14.680 --> 32:15.940
I came looking for you.

32:16.400 --> 32:18.240
You remember that killer named Bai Zhu?

32:18.240 --> 32:19.170
She got caught.

32:19.200 --> 32:20.750
Then one of the armed men
was about to torture her to death.

32:20.750 --> 32:22.240
I tried to stop him,

32:22.260 --> 32:24.110
but Bai Zhu killed him in an instant

32:24.110 --> 32:24.960
and then collapsed.

32:24.960 --> 32:25.480
I didn't know what else to do.

32:25.480 --> 32:26.750
So I dragged her into a lifeboat.

32:26.750 --> 32:27.790
But I didn't dare stay there.

32:27.790 --> 32:29.350
I was afraid she'd kill me
when she woke up.

32:29.350 --> 32:30.720
But I couldn't just leave her
on deck either.

32:30.720 --> 32:31.750
I was worried
someone else would get to her.

32:31.750 --> 32:32.240
I had no choice,

32:32.240 --> 32:33.640
so I came looking for you.

32:34.310 --> 32:34.680
Okay, okay.

32:34.680 --> 32:35.640
I get it now.

32:37.830 --> 32:39.190
Now we have two bodies.

32:41.200 --> 32:42.720
We need to find a place to hide.

32:42.720 --> 32:43.290
Hide.

32:43.480 --> 32:44.440
Okay, hide.

32:47.310 --> 32:48.610
Who are those guys?

32:49.400 --> 32:51.030
Miss Dong is in the cargo hold?

32:51.030 --> 32:53.400
I was going to finish off two killers
and bring back their bodies,

32:53.400 --> 32:54.660
but now I don't need to.

32:55.350 --> 32:56.350
The cargo hold...

32:57.480 --> 32:58.310
Are you okay?

33:01.960 --> 33:02.960
It's you.

33:02.960 --> 33:04.720
G-Go to the cargo hold.

33:05.160 --> 33:06.570
Everything is ready.

33:07.540 --> 33:09.200
We must kill that woman

33:09.640 --> 33:11.100
and complete the mission.

33:11.400 --> 33:13.260
We can't let anyone know about us.

33:13.440 --> 33:14.570
Everyone on the ship

33:15.270 --> 33:16.480
has to die.

33:17.480 --> 33:18.610
The cargo hold is...

33:19.960 --> 33:20.760
What's wrong?

33:21.240 --> 33:22.360
What's burning?

33:22.730 --> 33:23.990
Something is burning?

33:25.330 --> 33:28.260
That bastard just came to
blow up the electrical box.

33:29.680 --> 33:30.880
Why are you spitting?

33:31.720 --> 33:32.720
I'm out of blades.

33:32.720 --> 33:33.350
What do we do now?

33:33.350 --> 33:34.000
Retreat.

33:45.650 --> 33:46.820
Come on, let's go!

33:46.850 --> 33:47.790
Move! Move!

33:47.790 --> 33:48.400
Go, go, go!

33:48.400 --> 33:49.600
Go check out the door.

33:51.950 --> 33:53.130
Check out the door.

33:54.240 --> 33:55.860
I have no idea! Let's check!

33:56.000 --> 33:57.600
They must be here somewhere.

33:57.680 --> 33:58.860
Check upstairs.

33:59.030 --> 34:00.590
Check out the floor down there.

34:00.590 --> 34:01.960
Nobody!

34:02.000 --> 34:03.400
Nobody here!

34:39.630 --> 34:41.360
Your wound has torn open again.

34:43.320 --> 34:44.400
There are killers.

34:52.600 --> 34:55.530
Good God, how did we end up
in the cargo hold after all?

34:56.210 --> 34:56.880
No.

34:56.909 --> 34:58.360
We need to get out of here now.

34:58.360 --> 34:59.100
Bai Zhu said

34:59.590 --> 35:02.650
there are traps in the cargo hold.
It's very dangerous.

35:03.790 --> 35:04.990
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

35:04.990 --> 35:06.010
I just did.

35:06.230 --> 35:08.360
I was cut off halfway by the explosion.

35:12.080 --> 35:13.010
Stay close to me.

35:27.590 --> 35:29.590
Someone's there. Someone's there.

35:30.050 --> 35:30.880
A dead man.

35:34.880 --> 35:35.670
It was a man,

35:35.670 --> 35:36.570
not Miss Dong.

35:36.800 --> 35:39.000
Counting Bai Zhu,
that makes exactly two bodies.

35:39.000 --> 35:40.060
Carry the body out.

35:50.120 --> 35:50.810
No, no.

35:54.360 --> 35:55.150
Front left.

35:55.290 --> 35:56.290
Someone's there.

36:02.850 --> 36:03.780
There have to be

36:04.050 --> 36:06.510
at least dozens of people
in this cargo hold.

36:09.200 --> 36:11.060
Where is the killer closest to me?

36:15.700 --> 36:17.760
Front left, behind the cargo crates.

36:18.320 --> 36:19.400
Exact location.

36:21.280 --> 36:21.760
Just...

36:35.580 --> 36:36.580
Right over there.

36:38.610 --> 36:39.610
Right over there.

36:46.760 --> 36:48.490
Don't touch the wooden crates.

36:48.500 --> 36:50.960
There seems to be
something wrong with them.

38:04.000 --> 38:04.800
Plague,

38:04.800 --> 38:05.670
be careful!

38:05.670 --> 38:07.200
Many people are closing in.

39:31.390 --> 39:32.600
Zhang Ruipu?
